// Every exercise name in the Strong export, and the Lionheart movement it becomes: a movement
// base, the equipment, and an optional modifier. Edit this file to correct a mapping; the import
// reads it at build time, so `dotnet run` picks up a change without anything else to do.
//
// - "strong" is the name exactly as Strong exports it. Matching ignores case and surrounding
//   spaces, so `Low Bar Squat ` and `low bar squat` are the same entry.
// - Names, equipment and modifiers are matched against what the athlete already has the same way,
//   so an existing movement is reused rather than duplicated. Anything not there yet is created.
// - Several Strong names mapping to one movement is how variants and typos are folded together.
// - "unsure" marks a mapping that was a judgement call, and says why. The import lists every
//   unsure mapping it used, so none of them is applied silently. Delete the field once settled.
// - An exercise in the export with no entry here stops the import before anything is written.
//
// Correct a mapping before importing: an imported session is never re-read, so a correction made
// afterwards does not reach sessions already in the database.
